{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 3873464,
  "courseSlug": "nextjs-react-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25145978",
      "title": "Exploring Different Ways Of Structuring API Route Files",
      "lectureOrder": 325,
      "videoOrder": 302,
      "sourceHash": "5877264a6f4e0f7cc4f0e11f2f5a9733568b997b9d2cfa5d4e18093a3ed1d026",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.13,
          "end": 4.47,
          "en": "Now we know about API routes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.47,
          "end": 7.25,
          "en": "including dynamic API routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.25,
          "end": 8.97,
          "en": "Now it is worth a note that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.97,
          "end": 11.69,
          "en": "there are some alternatives to how we name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.69,
          "end": 15.41,
          "en": "and structure our files inside of the API folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.41,
          "end": 18.32,
          "en": "And those alternatives are equivalent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.32,
          "end": 20.4,
          "en": "to the different approaches we can use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.4,
          "end": 22.87,
          "en": "for regular pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.87,
          "end": 27.87,
          "en": "For example, you can also have catch-all dynamic API routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.09,
          "end": 31.49,
          "en": "by adding free dots in front of any placeholder name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.49,
          "end": 33.01,
          "en": "of your choice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.01,
          "end": 38.01,
          "en": "This will then not just handle requests to /API/some value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.93,
          "end": 42.45,
          "en": "but also to more segments you might have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.45,
          "end": 45.56,
          "en": "Equivalent to what you learned about regular pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.56,
          "end": 48.03,
          "en": "and catch-all pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.03,
          "end": 51.3,
          "en": "Now we don't need a catch-all dynamic API route here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.3,
          "end": 53.47,
          "en": "but it is worth knowing about it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.47,
          "end": 55.57,
          "en": "It's all important to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.57,
          "end": 60.01,
          "en": "how Next.js prioritizes these different files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.01,
          "end": 63.88,
          "en": "If we send the request to /API/feedback,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.88,
          "end": 68.2,
          "en": "it's decode into feedback.js file, it will be executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.2,
          "end": 71,
          "en": "Now that is not necessarily obvious",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71,
          "end": 73.66,
          "en": "because we have this dynamic API route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.66,
          "end": 78.66,
          "en": "So it could also be possible that requests to /API/feedback",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 78.69,
          "end": 83.27,
          "en": "are consumed by this file because feedback is simply treated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 83.27,
          "end": 87.6,
          "en": "as a concrete value for this feedback ID placeholder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 87.6,
          "end": 92.55,
          "en": "But Next.js is smart just as it is for regular pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 92.55,
          "end": 97.55,
          "en": "And if there is a more specific page for a given path value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 97.6,
          "end": 100.56,
          "en": "so since we have a feedback.js file in this case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 100.56,
          "end": 102.97999999999999,
          "en": "it will use that more specific file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 102.97999999999999,
          "end": 105.87,
          "en": "which makes more sense for this kind of path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 105.87,
          "end": 108.979,
          "en": "than the more generic dynamic file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 108.979,
          "end": 112.96000000000001,
          "en": "/API some value on the other hand would trigger",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 112.96000000000001,
          "end": 116.64,
          "en": "the code in the dynamic API route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 116.64,
          "end": 118.16,
          "en": "So that's just worth knowing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 118.16,
          "end": 120.3,
          "en": "It automatically works correctly here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 120.3,
          "end": 122.73,
          "en": "but it is important to be aware of the fact",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 122.73,
          "end": 126.913,
          "en": "that Next.js will do this prioritization for you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 128.406,
          "end": 130.49,
          "en": "Now, another important thing to know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 130.49,
          "end": 132.44,
          "en": "is that you have some flexibility",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 132.44,
          "end": 135.76,
          "en": "regarding how you structure your files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 135.76,
          "end": 139.94,
          "en": "You can add a feedback.js file in the API folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 139.94,
          "end": 144.12,
          "en": "to support requests to /API/feedback.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 144.12,
          "end": 147.5,
          "en": "Alternatively, just as with the regular pages,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 147.5,
          "end": 151.71,
          "en": "you could also add a feedback sub folder in the API folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 151.71,
          "end": 154.57,
          "en": "and then move to file in there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 154.57,
          "end": 158,
          "en": "and rename it to index.js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 158,
          "end": 160.42000000000002,
          "en": "And here vscode is asking me",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 160.42000000000002,
          "end": 163.48,
          "en": "whether it should automatically update all imports",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 163.48,
          "end": 165.32,
          "en": "that pointed at this file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 165.32,
          "end": 166.57,
          "en": "and I will say, yes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 166.57,
          "end": 169.59,
          "en": "If you don't get the prompt or you chose, no,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 169.59,
          "end": 174.28,
          "en": "you should manually update those import puffs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 174.28,
          "end": 176.28,
          "en": "So that is the alternative.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 176.28,
          "end": 179.65,
          "en": "A file named index.js in the feedback folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 179.65,
          "end": 182.26,
          "en": "in the API folder is the equivalent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 182.26,
          "end": 186.39,
          "en": "to having a feedback.js file inside of the API folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 186.39,
          "end": 189.77,
          "en": "just as it works for regular pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 189.77,
          "end": 193.87,
          "en": "We can also move our feedback ID js file in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 193.87,
          "end": 195.01,
          "en": "But if we do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 195.01,
          "end": 198.836,
          "en": "that of course also changes the way our API works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 198.836,
          "end": 201.62,
          "en": "Previously, since feedback ID,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 201.62,
          "end": 206.39,
          "en": "this dynamic API route was directly in the API folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 206.39,
          "end": 210.13,
          "en": "previously /API some value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 210.13,
          "end": 214.5,
          "en": "triggered the code in this feedback ID file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 214.5,
          "end": 216.86,
          "en": "Now, since we're in a feedback sub folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 216.86,
          "end": 221.69,
          "en": "it's actually /API/feedback/some value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 221.69,
          "end": 223.483,
          "en": "that triggers the code in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 224.75,
          "end": 228.13,
          "en": "Now that is actually a path that makes more sense to me.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 228.13,
          "end": 229.72,
          "en": "It's more descriptive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 229.72,
          "end": 232.92000000000002,
          "en": "it's clearer that some requests sent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 232.92000000000002,
          "end": 236.3,
          "en": "to /API/feedback/some value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 236.3,
          "end": 239.67000000000002,
          "en": "should fetch more details for a single feedback",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 239.67000000000002,
          "end": 243.19,
          "en": "than if we have just /API/F1.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 243.19,
          "end": 246.74,
          "en": "That doesn't tell us that it's about fetching feedback data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 246.74,
          "end": 249.2,
          "en": "if we just look at this kind of path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 249.2,
          "end": 251.57,
          "en": "And hence it will keep this structure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 251.57,
          "end": 254.7,
          "en": "of having these square bracket feedback ID file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 254.7,
          "end": 258.68,
          "en": "inside of the feedback folder inside of the API folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 258.68,
          "end": 261.92,
          "en": "However, that means that in the index.js file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 261.92,
          "end": 264.75,
          "en": "in the feedback folder, in the regular pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 264.75,
          "end": 266.92,
          "en": "So in the feedback page component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 266.92,
          "end": 269.82,
          "en": "we also need to update this URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 269.82,
          "end": 274.82,
          "en": "and send our request to /API/feedback/some ID,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 275.32,
          "end": 278.533,
          "en": "because I changed that structure in the API's folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 279.68,
          "end": 282.84000000000003,
          "en": "And now it looks like I broke some imports as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 282.84000000000003,
          "end": 285.783,
          "en": "Yes, here we should import from the index file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 287.01,
          "end": 288.543,
          "en": "And now that works again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 289.84000000000003,
          "end": 292.68,
          "en": "So if I now reload, that all works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 292.68,
          "end": 294.723,
          "en": "that works, looking good.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 296.06,
          "end": 299.13,
          "en": "So that is how you can also structure your files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 299.13,
          "end": 303.03,
          "en": "and folders in the API folder, in the pages folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 303.03,
          "end": 306.09,
          "en": "It essentially works just as it does",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 306.09,
          "end": 307.673,
          "en": "for regular pages.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
